{
  "requirement": "Source providers can override parsing, text search, and structural search.\nThe SDK supplies defaults for all three, so listing, reading, and a supplied\nlanguage registry suffice to support them.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.sources.provider_defaults`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n- A provider can override parsing, text search and structural search.\n- The SDK supplies a default for each of the three.\n- A provider that implements only listing and reading, plus a supplied language registry, is enough to support all three.\n\n**Default parsing**\n- `tests/sources.rs#fn[defaults_use_provider_primitives_and_keep_one_parse_snapshot]` uses `Memory`. Its `SourceProvider` impl defines only `list` and `read`.\n  - It calls the default `parse` and asserts the parsed text, the outline content, and exactly one read.\n  - It asserts the parse keeps its snapshot after a newer read.\n- `fn[list_read_only_provider_supports_selected_language_parse_and_structural_search]` uses `Primitives`. Its impl also defines only `list` and `read`.\n  - It parses a resource with an explicit language and checks that the outline resolves `fn[provided]`.\n  - It checks that an explicit language wins over the file extension.\n  - It checks that, with no explicit language, the extension (`.rs`) selects the language.\n\n**Default text search**\n- The same `Memory` test calls the default `search_text`. It asserts `complete`, two matches, the line number, and the context excerpt.\n- It also asserts the event order `[\"src/one.txt\", \"src/one.txt\", \"list\", \"src/one.txt\"]`, which shows the default search is built from the provider's `list` and `read` primitives.\n\n**Default structural search**\n- The `Primitives` test calls the default `search_structure` with the registry. It asserts one complete match with the right selector, excerpt and resource.\n- It checks that a malformed rule is an error.\n- It checks that a language mismatch gives an empty complete result.\n- It checks that an unknown language is an error.\n\n**Overrides**\n- `fn[structural_search_uses_overridden_parses_their_snapshot_and_requested_scope]` uses `CachedParse`, which overrides `parse`. The default structural search uses that override, the test counts parse calls, and it checks the limit and completeness cases.\n- The tests never override `search_text` or `search_structure` themselves. The requirement says providers \"can\" override, which only states a capability, and the parse override is tested. I don't count this as a gap.\n\n**Agent-level test**\n- `tests/agent.rs#fn[source_tools_keep_search_discovery_separate_from_delivered_source_reads]` runs `search_text` through `LocalSources` with only the primitives, and it is also marked for this requirement.\n\nNothing in the requirement's text is left untested, and I found no marking gaps.",
  "references": "f81af2930dbcb6e08cb02303b0bab8c8c984cacdc898527c7b3e2bc6e3c399b9",
